.title  The ground stops being flat: relief, and what is behind a hill
.what   Every node of the lattice takes its height from the island - and one shift doubles it, because 1024 units between nodes against 1110 at the highest point is why it looked flat. Then hidden lines in 320 bytes, one a screen column, drawn from the eye outwards. Measured, hiding is FASTER than a plain line; the frames it costs went on leaving lesson 8's patched one behind
.tier   LESSON
.main   RELIEF.ASM
.build  FASM RELIEF.ASM RELIEF.COM
.run    RELIEF.COM
.uses   IMUL IDIV SHL SHR STOSB REP XOR CMP JLE JGE IN OUT CLI STI IRET
